# Build-time de-identification evidence. NEVER committed.
#
# .temper/evidence/deident-terms.txt is the list of strings this template was
# scrubbed of. Committing it would ship a curated enumeration of precisely what
# the template claims to have removed — a worse leak than a stray mention,
# because it is organised, and because it is the first file a reader opens to
# audit whether the extraction was clean.
#
# tools/check-deidentified.sh is deliberately term-agnostic (`--terms <file>`)
# so that it is subject to its own sweep with no self-exclusion. A check that
# must exempt itself to pass is not a check.
.temper/evidence/

# Adopters: put your own fork's term list here. tools/check-deidentified.sh
# defaults to this path.
.deident-terms

# The build prompt this template was extracted against. It is the requirements
# input for this build, not template content — it names the source project by
# design, so it can never pass the de-identification sweep. It stays on disk for
# the operator; it must never be tracked.
/agentsdlcrepoprompt.md

# Reference-stack build output — examples/ is the bundled example product
# (tasks.md Task 23); tools/init.sh offers to delete the whole directory once an
# adopter's own product is wired in.
examples/backend/target/
examples/frontend/node_modules/
examples/frontend/dist/
examples/frontend/coverage/
examples/frontend/reports/
examples/frontend/playwright-report/
examples/frontend/test-results/
examples/frontend/e2e/.cache/
examples/backend/archunit_store/*.tmp

.DS_Store

# scratch dirs used by the round-trip transcript
.scratch/

*.tsbuildinfo
